SECTION: HEADER (The Fast-Travel Anchor)

Vibe: A persistent, living artifact. Not a traditional navigation bar.
Goal: Serve as a functional "escape hatch" for recruiters to skip the narrative
and find your contact info, while acting as a visual anchor that proves your
state-management and 3D rendering skills.

THE CONTAINER & ARCHITECTURE

Positioning: Fixed (or sticky) to the top of the viewport. It must persist
across all sections (Future, Air, Water, Earth) until the final Footer snap.

Z-Index: Extremely high (above all WebGL canvases, fluid simulations, and
cave darkness overlays) to ensure it is always clickable.

Layout: Minimalist structure. The t.tofu logo sits in the top left. The main navigation links (Projects, Skills, Contact) align perfectly in the center of the header to establish immediate context.

THE ARTIFACT (TotoTofu Logo)

Geometry: A 3D or pseudo-3D geometric block representing a piece of tofu.

Graphic Detail: The top one-third of the block features a stylized, abstract
"sauce" wave graphic.

Label (Optional): A tiny, minimal label beneath or beside it reading t.tofu
using the Space Grotesk font (Accent/UI font).

SCROLL-LINKED ANIMATIONS (Material Degradation)

The artifact does not stay the same; its material and texture dynamically
change/degrade based on which section (era) the user is currently viewing.

State 1: Future / Fire (Hero & About Sections)

Material: Polished Chrome, Frosted Glass, or Neon.

Colors: Sleek whites/grays with a subtle digital amber/plasma glow.

State 2: Modern / Air (Projects Section)

Material: Matte Silver / Clean Ceramic.

Colors: Cool slate and muted gray.

State 3: Water (Skills Section)

Material: Sunken, oxidized metal or deep-sea glass.

Colors: Dark indigo with bioluminescent aqua/teal edge highlights.

State 4: Earth (Contact Section)

Material: Ancient, moss-covered stone or heavily carved dark wood.

Colors: Shadowy browns and charcoals. It reacts dynamically to the user's
flashlight cursor.

INTERACTIVE ANIMATIONS (Hover & Click)

Hover State (The Tease):

Action: When the cursor hovers over the artifact, it triggers a smooth,
physics-based 3D rotation (e.g., a slight tilt on the X and Y axes tracking
the mouse position).

Visual Cue: A subtle tooltip or glowing text appears reading:
[ Fast-Travel to Contact ].

Click State (The Escape Hatch):

Action: Clicking the artifact completely overrides the standard scroll behavior.

Animation: Triggers a "fast-travel" tunnel or warp effect. The camera rapidly
zooms through the Z-axis (or rapidly scrubs the timeline), bypassing the
Air and Water sections entirely.

Destination: Hard-drops the user directly into the pitch-black Earth (Cave)
section, landing precisely at the torch bracket.

TECHNICAL UX NOTE

To maintain high performance, the material transitions (Chrome -> Stone) should
ideally be handled via a shader material (if using Three.js) interpolating
between textures based on the scroll progress (0 to 1), rather than mounting
and unmounting entirely different 3D models.